#1157 is fixed and committed as eda208f2. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass. Along the way I found that one of the ticket's premises is wrong (details below).

What changed
• One table of limits (GOOGLE_PUBLISHED_LIMITS in src/providers.rs): six rows, each with the URL of that model's own Google page, which I read today. All six say 1,048,576 input and 65,536 output tokens. The ticket counted seven ids, but gemini-3.1-pro-preview is already a yoagent 0.27.4 preset, so it needs no row. None of the offered ids is left on a guess. A test-only copy of the same id list is gone, and its test now reads this table.
• Run path (agent_builder.rs): the google branch uses the row whenever yoagent has no preset. The output-ceiling check reads the row too, so max_tokens above 65,536 now gets the "exceeds the declared ceiling" warning.
• `/model info` (commands_info.rs): it reads the same table, and the separately typed Gemini window is deleted. It now also prints Output: from the same source. A Gemini id Google doesn't list now shows the window as "unknown" instead of a guessed 1M.
• Docs: docs/src/configuration/models.md lists the six ids and their published limits.

Tests
• New tests in src/google_limits_tests.rs check that:
  • every offered google id has either a preset or a row, never both;
  • the run path and /model info give the same numbers;
  • gemini-zzz still gets the guess;
  • a user's max_tokens still wins.
• I updated five older tests: they used gemini-2.5-* as their example of a model with no known limits, which is no longer true. They now use ids Google doesn't list.
• Check that the new test catches a missing row: I deleted the gemini-2.5-pro row and the test failed by name ("google offers gemini-2.5-pro: no yoagent preset and no GOOGLE_PUBLISHED_LIMITS row"). I restored the row in the same command and it went green again.
• Binary probe:
  • --model gemini-2.5-pro -p hi: no guessed-limits warning.
  • --model gemini-zzz -p hi: the warning still fires.
  • model info gemini-2.5-pro: shows 1.0M context and 65k output.

The premise that's wrong: the ticket said the 8192 default "silently truncates long answers". From reading yoagent's code (I haven't sent a real request), the Google provider only sends an output limit when the user has set max_tokens (google.rs:733, agent.rs:1632). If they haven't, nothing is sent and Google uses its own default. So the old guess changed yoyo's context budget, its warnings and /model info, but it didn't cut off replies. The commit message gives the code citations.

Follow-up: that means the warning still shown for unknown Gemini ids, "every reply is capped at 8192 output tokens", is also likely false. I filed it as #1158 rather than commenting on #1157, because this push closes #1157. #1158 includes a cheap check: a stub server that captures the request and confirms whether the limit is sent.

agent_builder.rs is now 5011 lines against 4977 recorded, which is within the size test's 100-line allowance, so I didn't update the recorded count.

